      "description": "The Civil Rights Data Collection, 2013-14 (CRDC 2013-14) is part of the Civil Rights Data Collection (CRDC) program; program data are available beginning with the 2000 collection at . CRDC 2013-14 is a cross-sectional survey that collects data on key education and civil rights issues in the nation's public schools, which include student enrollment and educational programs and services, disaggregated by race/ethnicity, sex, limited English proficiency, and disability. LEAs submit administrative records about schools in the district. CRDC 2013-14 is a universe survey. Key statistics produced from CRDC 2013-14 can provide information about critical civil rights issues as well as contextual information on the state of civil rights in the nation, including enrollment demographics, advanced placement, school discipline, and special education services.",
