      "description": "The Public School Principals' Perceptions of Their School Facilities, Fall 2005 (FRSS 88), is a study that is part of the Fast Response Survey System (FRSS) program; program data is available since 1998-99 at . FRSS 88 (https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/frss/) is a cross-sectional survey that collects and report data on principals' perceptions of their school facilities at the elementary and secondary levels. Principals in sampled schools received questionnaires regarding the condition of their school facilities. Respondents had the option of completing paper or web-based questionnaires. The study's response weighted rate was 91 percent. Key statistics produced from FRSS 88 will provide current information about principals' satisfaction with various environmental factors in their schools and the extent to which they perceive those factors as interfering with the ability of the school to deliver instruction.",
